WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.720
That’s right, it’s that time again!

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:08.380
We’re recalibrating, rebooting, and hitting
restart on our infamous Anom-O-Tron 6000,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:13.190
the specialized supercomputer we developed
to simulate improbable scenarios between the

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.119
SCP Foundation’s various anomalies, and
any other character from any other universe

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:20.080
you could possibly imagine.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.530
On today’s agenda?

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:26.269
What do you think would happen if John Wick,
the notorious hitman, highly trained in all

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:31.599
forms of combat, was up against an enemy that
won’t go down in a single shot: an undead

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:33.880
menace known as SCP-008?

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.700
Well, we’re about to hit the button and
find out!

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.510
Either by a pure, unpredictable instance of
human error, or through the act of some twisted

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:47.050
karmic fate, the SCP Foundation had an outbreak
on their hands.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:53.129
A sample of the complex prion, a virus known
as SCP-008, had leaked.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:57.520
The Foundation had hoped to keep the existence
of the disease highly classified, even among

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.149
its own personnel.

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:03.910
Their fear had been that some hostile force
would attempt to synthesize or even weaponize

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:09.870
SCP-008; after all, the disease had a one
hundred percent rate of both infection and

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:10.930
lethality.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:17.490
It killed anything it came into contact with…
or at least, it killed them, to begin with.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:22.010
Before long, everyone in the Foundation facility
that had been exposed to the leaking sample

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.689
or SCP-008’s already infected victims was
dead.

00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:29.050
Flu-like symptoms were followed swiftly by
a coma.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:33.619
However, the disease hijacked the bodies of
all those it had passed to, reactivating the

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:36.490
motor functions of their corpses and turning
them into…

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.049
well, you can already guess.

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:44.560
No one was safe, even the Mobile Task Force
on the scene were soon infected with SCP-008.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.340
They had been a squad of rookies and fresh-faced
new recruits, sent in by the Foundation under

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.030
the assumption that an outbreak of this sort
should have been easy to contain…

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.030
it wasn’t.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.840
The entire facility was soon overrun, the
bodies of Foundation researchers, security

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.729
officers and MTF troops reanimated after their
deaths, now jostling around in search of survivors

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.530
to pass SCP-008 on to.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:11.160
“That should hold them!”

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.690
Doctor Alto Clef yelled, locking tight the
entrance to the watchtower.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:18.220
“This really is another fine mess, Clef!”

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.790
his colleague, Doctor Gears, replied in frustration.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.410
“Our MTF backup are all down, we could be
the last two people on site and we’re locked

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.360
in a tower with only one entry door.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.390
Tell me, what the hell are we supposed to
do now?”

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.750
“Will you relax?”

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:32.750
Clef insisted.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.440
“Don’t worry, there’s someone we can
call to get us out of this jam.”

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:41.040
“Don’t say ‘I know a guy’,” Gears
sighed, as his fellow researcher gave a wide

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.860
grin and reached for his cell phone.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:48.659
A few moments later, and only a matter of
miles away, another phone started ringing.

00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:53.790
Its owner, a man in a dark, all-black tailored
suit with a shadowy shirt and tie to match,

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:57.420
reached into his pocket and lifted his cell
phone to his ear.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.190
“Good evening, I apologize for calling you
at this hour,” came the unmistakable voice

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.709
of Charon, the concierge of the New York Continental
Hotel.

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:08.700
“That’s quite alright,” replied the
suited man.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.519
“We received a call asking for your whereabouts,
sir.”

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:12.519
“A job?”

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:14.520
the man asked in a monotone voice.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.319
“Indeed,” Charon replied.

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:17.319
“Up front?”

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:20.940
“I’m afraid not,” the hotel’s receptionist
answered sympathetically.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.960
“The contract is only in exchange for payment
upon completion.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.170
The man who made the call was very insistent,
he said he will be in no position to pay until

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.240
the job is done.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:36.420
But he asked for you specifically, and told
us he’d be grateful for your assistance.”

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.310
The man on the end of the line sighed.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.310
“Where?”

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:42.340
“Oh, don’t worry, sir,” the friendly
concierge replied.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.069
“We’re sending a car for you.”

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:47.879
At that precise moment, a yellow New York
cab pulled up to the sidewalk.

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:53.250
“Best of luck, Mr. Wick,” Charon said,
before hanging up the call.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.629
Straightening his suit, the infamous hitman
John Wick climbed into the back of the taxi

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:00.310
as it sped off towards its destination.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:05.489
Arriving at a complex upstate, far off the
beaten track, John examined his surroundings

00:04:05.489 --> 00:04:09.050
while the car inched closer to the nearest
part of the facility.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:13.709
His years of training as an assassin, under
the tutelage of the Rusk Roma, had given him

00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:18.859
an instinctive spatial awareness, one that
came in handy in his line of work.

00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:23.390
But even then, John couldn’t have predicted
that something would come leaping down from

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.820
above, crashing through the cab's windshield.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:31.050
The car's hood buckled under the impact, fragments
of glass spraying everywhere as an arm cracked

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.350
the front window.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:37.080
The thing snarled and gurgled like a wild
animal as it reached for the taxi driver,

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.110
gripping his arm.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:43.020
It pulled him by the wrist, biting down, causing
him to scream in intense pain.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:47.490
Meanwhile, John had already moved with lightning-fast
reflexes and sprung out of the backseat.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:52.660
He hadn’t had a chance to assess the threat,
his instincts told him his best option was

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.930
to put some distance between himself and whatever
had just attacked the car.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:00.259
Then, he’d be able to get a better idea
what he was dealing with.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:05.100
The job description he’d been hired for
had been light on details, John’s mystery

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.780
employer only referring to it as ‘A clean-up
operation.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.350
Sprinting towards the facility, John slammed
the door behind him.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:17.160
He pulled off his belt from around his waist
and wrapped it tightly around the door handles;

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.750
it would hold, for now.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:23.160
It was only when he turned around that he
saw a few clustered groups of figures shuffling

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.840
around inside the building’s atrium.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.760
The nearest gaggle were close enough that
it was easy for John to make out their pale

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:35.039
skin, sunken eyes and cheeks, the unnatural
twitches and erratic movements they were making

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:38.160
as the creatures turned to look back at him.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.440
“Zombies,” John Wick muttered under his
breath.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.760
“That’s unexpected.”

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.979
The nearby trio of SCP-008 infectees looked
like they were about to make a dash towards

00:05:45.979 --> 00:05:48.370
him, so John moved first.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.690
He raced towards a nearby corridor, hearing
that the three zombies were already chasing

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:53.690
after him.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:58.259
Their shambling footsteps had quickly become
an animalistic charge, their limbs only able

00:05:58.259 --> 00:06:02.500
to move after death thanks to the virus that
they were infected with.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:06.889
Turning a corner, John Wick took cover, his
shoulder pressed to the wall.

00:06:06.889 --> 00:06:11.900
He drew his pistol from its holster underneath
his suit jacket, and stood in a battle-ready

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:12.900
stance.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:17.250
The second he saw one of the zombie’s faces
appear around the corner, he raised his weapon

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:22.199
and fired, swooping around out of his hiding
place to fire another two shots.

00:06:22.199 --> 00:06:25.100
All three hit center mass, right through the
chests.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:30.000
The noise would no doubt have drawn the attention
of the other SCP-008s in the building, but

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.330
for now, the three that had been on his tail
dropped to the floor…

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.310
only to start getting back up again.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.440
John wasn’t used to his targets standing
to their feet after he’d already fired at

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:45.849
them, and as the nearest of the zombies staggered
back to his level, he lifted his firearm again.

00:06:45.849 --> 00:06:49.720
Before his finger could compress enough force
on the trigger, though, the undead abomination

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.060
took a wild, flailing swipe at him.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:57.000
The SCP-008 instance knocked the weapon out
of John’s hand, causing it to clatter to

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.949
the ground while it reared back its other
arm for a second strike.

00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:05.530
Catching the blow, John Wick displayed his
incredible reflexes and mastery of martial

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.530
arts.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:10.639
He delivered a series of precise punches and
chops, deploying a combination of Brazilian

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:15.860
Jiu-Jitsu, Aikido, and Krav Maga to try and
knock the snarling monster down.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:20.110
With each hit, he was careful to avoid the
zombie’s mouth; having seen one bite the

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:26.200
cab driver earlier, John had assessed that
SCP-008 could be transmitted through biting.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.660
And he was correct.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:32.580
Exposure to mucous membranes of bodily fluids
of an infected individual was what allowed

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.410
the virus to spread.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:39.120
One of the other SCP-008 zombies that were
still in the process of climbing back up swiped

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.310
John’s legs out from underneath him.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:45.570
The master assassin toppled over, landing
on his back with the weight of the first monster

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:50.160
still on top of him, while the second clawed
at his tapered suit pants.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.190
Seconds before it could snap its teeth down
on his ankle, John pulled back his leg and

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:59.409
shot it back out in a devastating bicycle
kick that sent the second zombie reeling into

00:07:59.409 --> 00:08:03.430
the third, which was still trying to get back
up after its earlier gunshot.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:07.349
But, the first of the creatures were still
bearing down on him.

00:08:07.349 --> 00:08:11.910
Mustering as much of his peak physical strength
as he needed, John Wick held the zombie at

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:16.629
bay, blocking it with one arm, stopping it
from getting close enough to bite him.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:21.409
His eyes darted around, looking for something,
anything he could use.

00:08:21.409 --> 00:08:26.159
That was one of John’s most enviable and
impressive skills, one that had made him so

00:08:26.159 --> 00:08:29.229
renowned as the legend of the assassin world.

00:08:29.229 --> 00:08:34.899
In the hands of John Wick, any ordinary, everyday
object could be a lethal weapon.

00:08:34.899 --> 00:08:38.970
Reaching out with his other hand, John felt
his fingertips brush against something metal.

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:41.769
It was so close, just out of reach.

00:08:41.769 --> 00:08:45.529
On top of him, the zombie flailed its arms,
trying to claw at him.

00:08:45.529 --> 00:08:50.480
Lifting both legs, in a fluid, balletic motion,
John Wick kicked the creature off of him,

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:55.010
crawling towards the nearby object and grabbing
it, just as the zombie started to approach

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.010
again.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:00.100
With a swing and a loud, metallic clang, the
heavy fire extinguisher collided with the

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.890
SCP-008 infectee’s head.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:07.780
The force of the blow caused it to drop in
an instant, landing in a heap on the floor.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.820
John waited a second to see if it would get
back up again… but it was still.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.030
The other two zombies suddenly dashed towards
the infamous hitman, only for their prey to

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:21.080
duck and weave effortlessly between their
aggressive clawing swipes, bashing his makeshift

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.850
weapon against their heads like a battering
ram against a door.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:30.190
All three were down, but the entire facility
was still crawling with a mass of the reanimated

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.190
monstrosities.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:36.000
Calmly, John smoothed his suit and straightened
up his shirt and tie, walking with the fire

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:41.690
extinguisher in hand back down the corridor
towards the sounds of more SCP-008 zombies

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:42.960
snarling.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.200
They were next.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:49.320
The Baba Yaga would use anything he found
to take down each and every one of them, until

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.310
not one was left standing.

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:55.390
It didn’t matter if all he had to hand was
a fire extinguisher, or one of the fallen

00:09:55.390 --> 00:10:01.060
security officer’s batons, or even just
a tiny pencil… nothing would make it out

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:02.920
of that facility alive.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.370
He just had to go for the head.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:10.790
Still trapped in the watchtower, Doctor Clef
and Doctor Gears had long since grown irritated

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.380
with each other’s company.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.980
They had no security feeds, no way of knowing
what was going on within the overrun Foundation

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:18.089
facility.

00:10:18.089 --> 00:10:21.880
For a while, the pair of researchers had been
toying with the idea of climbing out of a

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:26.400
window and scaling down the side of the tower,
but gave up on that plan when they realised

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:30.899
that they’d only be dropping back into a
horde of SCP-008 zombies.

00:10:30.899 --> 00:10:35.470
A sudden explosion erupted from one corner
of the complex, causing Gears and Clef to

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.360
direct their attention towards it.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.300
From their elevation, they could see the ground
below was littered with the bodies of the

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:47.510
SCP-008 infectees, rendered lifeless once
again by significant cranial trauma.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:53.490
In short, something had been bashing the zombies
in the head… or someone.

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:58.920
The sound of a banging against the locked
watchtower door startled both Foundation scientists.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:02.420
Instantly they thought that the zombies had
made their way up the steps and found the

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:06.070
two researchers; easy prey, trapped in a cage.

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:11.230
The heavy thud against the metal door repeated,
then there was a pause, deafening, tense silence

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.510
filling the room.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:16.410
A polite knock came from the other side of
the watchtower entrance.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:19.320
Cautiously, Clef approached to unlock it.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:23.580
Standing in the doorway as it opened was a
single figure, panting with exhaustion but

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.089
still nowhere near beaten.

00:11:25.089 --> 00:11:30.400
He looked out at Bright and Clef from his
dark hair, a stern expression on his face.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:34.670
Neither one of the researchers could believe
he was still alive, still uninfected.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:40.459
But then again, he was the one and only John
Wick… the Baba Yaga.

00:11:40.459 --> 00:11:47.360
Now go check out“BOBA FETT VS SCP-610 THE
FLESH THAT HATES” and “SCP-076 Able VS

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:50.290
Chainsaw Man...Who Has The Most Lethal Weapon?”

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:52.189
for more epic out of universe What Ifs!

